<title>UK: BES Finance sets $200 million step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>BES Finance sets $200 million step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan, UBS (books) and Banco Espirito Santo</p>
<p> BORROWER   BES FINANCE LTD</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  EANCO ESPIRITO SANTO ET COMERCIAL DE LISBOA SA</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY  **PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **+0.625    PAY DATE    26.JUN.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY BAA1	ISS PRICE  99.766    FULL FEES   0.625</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   BBB	 REOFFER    99.766</p>
<p> NOTES    **CALLABLE JUN.02 WHEN COUPON STEPS UP TO 3M LIBOR</p>
<p>		PLUS 2.125 PCT</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10</p>
<p>SALE LIMITS US/UK/CI/PT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  0.375     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
